> like to keep cache's in Sokoban?

One of them, probably.  Any locked room or otherwise walled-off space
on a non-teleport level, such as the portal room on Ludios, will work
just as well, but Sokoban happens to be the earliest such level.

Another reason is that, being a dead-end branch level, there's no need
for you to spend time time there for other reasons.  The less time you
spend on a level, the less monsters are generated there -- and the
less time you spend on a stash level _without_ standing on your stash,
the less likely any of them is to stumble across it.

The Sokoban levels are also small, meaning that any monsters that do
get generated are easy to hunt down.  Also, one tends to find quite a
bit of food and useful gear in Soko, which makes it a good place to
start an early stash.

Later in the game, the Wizard quest artifact makes a stash on the
bottom level of Soko particularly convenient for those having it.

However, to return to the original subject, it's worth noting that
xorns are one of the relatively few monsters this setup won't protect
you against.  They can't phase through the Sokoban walls, but they can
pass the boulder just fine.  They do respect Elbereth, however.

